## Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url>
```

### 2. Navigate to the project directory

```bash
cd student-management-system
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

### 4. Install Axios

If Axios is not already installed:

```bash
npm install axios
```

### 5. Start the development server

```bash
npm run dev
```

The React application will normally be available at:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

## Backend API

This frontend expects a backend server running at:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

### API Endpoints

| Method   | Endpoint        | Description        |
| -------- | --------------- | ------------------ |
| `GET`    | `/students`     | Fetch all students |
| `POST`   | `/students`     | Add a new student  |
| `PUT`    | `/students/:id` | Update a student   |
| `DELETE` | `/students/:id` | Delete a student   |

### Student Object

The application uses the following student structure:

```json
{
  "id": "101",
  "name": "John Doe",
  "course": "Computer Science"
}
```

## Application Flow

### Fetch Students

When the application loads, `useEffect()` calls:

```javascript
axios.get(BASE_URL + '/students')
```

The returned student data is stored in the `students` state.

### Add Student

When the form is submitted without an active edit:

```javascript
axios.post(BASE_URL + '/students', {
  id,
  name,
  course
})
```

### Update Student

When editing an existing student:

```javascript
axios.put(BASE_URL + `/students/${editId}`, {
  id,
  name,
  course
})
```

### Delete Student

Clicking the **Delete** button sends:

```javascript
axios.delete(BASE_URL + `/students/${studentId}`)
```

After every create, update, or delete operation, the student list is fetched again to display the latest data.

## React State

The application uses React's `useState` hook to manage:

```javascript
const [id, setId] = useState('')
const [name, setName] = useState('')
const [course, setCourse] = useState('')
const [students, setStudents] = useState([])
const [editId, setEditId] = useState(null)
```

| State      | Purpose                                   |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `id`       | Stores the student ID                     |
| `name`     | Stores the student name                   |
| `course`   | Stores the student's course               |
| `students` | Stores the list of students               |
| `editId`   | Tracks the student currently being edited |

## Edit Functionality

Clicking **Edit** loads the selected student's information into the form:

```javascript
function editStudent(student) {
  setId(student.id)
  setName(student.name)
  setCourse(student.course)
  setEditId(student.id)
}
```

The form button changes from **Submit** to **Update** while editing.

## Delete Functionality

Clicking **Delete** removes the selected student from the backend and refreshes the student list.

